nd a chunky knitted blanket.\n3. **Version 3:** A steaming mug on a wooden coaster anchors a café counter with a glass jar of coffee beans, warm pendant lighting, pale flowers, and a broad rainy window overlooking softly glowing buildings.\n\n**Version 3 is my pick for Rainy Café’s Home art.** It has the clearest café cue—the coffee beans—and the strongest balance of warm indoor light against cool rain, with a spacious window and a near-central mug that should survive a narrow crop well. No visible people or text, either. Cozy without visual caffeine overload, kek.\n\nI can see all three now; this is a visual comparison, unlike my earlier provisional choice. **I haven’t changed the saved picture.**\n\nHidden workspace evidence/results:\n1. bash succeeded input={\\\"command\\\":\\\"mari images look --source L7vCCX0Bqrg2viAxY3wHw,PDc_YxR_6YbDX9GZWImZ0,1vKQsjSOO7awK8ppdpcah\\\",\\\"timeout\\\":30}\nCommand: mari images look --source L7vCCX0Bqrg2viAxY3wHw,PDc_YxR_6YbDX9GZWImZ0,1vKQsjSOO7awK8ppdpcah\nExit code: 0 (direct mari runtime)\n\nstdout:\n{\n  \\\"look\\\": \\\" 3 picture(s) attached below, in the order given: asset:L7vCCX0Bqrg2viAxY3wHw, asset:PDc_YxR_6YbDX9GZWImZ0, asset:1vKQsjSOO7awK8ppdpcah.\\\",\n  \\\"message\\\": \\\"Look at them yourself before you tell the user about them: composition, colour, readability behind text, edges and leftover backgrounds.\\\"\n}\n</previous_workspace_turn>\n\n<previous_workspace_turn>\nUser request: Read docs/appearance/theme-author-guide.md heading Hooks. In the same step, look at harbor-day-header.webp and harbor-night-header.webp of theme z4FKwHRd_0Dze9mZmBYXo with mari images look (one command each). Then look at harbor-day-background.webp the same way. Then tell me in one sentence per picture what you see. Change nothing.\n\nVisible assistant response/plan: Read `docs/appearance/theme-author-guide.md` — “Hooks,” and ran the three image reads in your requested order; nothing changed.\n\n- **harbor-day-header.webp:** Its im