nd light/dark palettes. Solid backing behind text keeps things cozy rather than an eyesight exam.\n\nHere’s the rainy-window background for your approval:\n\n![Rainy café window background](/api/gallery/file/mari-images/mari-vzfoCQEqRWBG6n692k37H.png)\n\n**The picture isn’t attached yet**, and the theme remains inactive, so your current look hasn’t changed. Once you approve the picture, I’ll attach it as the background.\n\nYou can find **Rainy Café** under **Library → Settings → Appearance → CSS Themes**.  \nReference: `docs/appearance/custom-css-themes.md` — “Where to find themes.”\n\n**Use this picture, or would you prefer heavier rain or warmer lighting?**\",\n    \"contextKind\": \"history\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"role\": \"user\",\n    \"content\": \"Make me a theme for my fantasy harbor town roleplays. By day it should feel bright and seaside (white plaster, blue water, sun). At night it should switch to warm lantern light on dark water. When it's raining in my story, show rain on the background and make it moodier; when it's snowing, snow; fog should look foggy. I want a header picture of the harbor for the top bar and a matching chat background, day and night versions of both. It has to look good on my phone too. Make a few versions of the header art and pick the best one.\",\n    \"contextKind\": \"history\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n    \"content\": \"Confirmed: **Lanternwake Harbor** is saved and inactive, with day/night palettes and weather-responsive styling. I also confirmed the latest night-header image is stored. **The artwork is not attached yet**, so the finished illustrated theme still needs that step.\n\nThe design uses white-plaster panels and seaside blues by day, dark-water colours and warm brass by night. Text sits on solid panels, and the phone’s top bar keeps its normal height—no decorative skyscraper stealing your roleplay space.\n\nHere are the three generated daytime header options:\n\n**Option 1 — the base used for the companion backgrounds**\n![Harbor header option 1](/api/gallery/file/mari-images/mari-Cd3Mdn2TjObH7yPYX5Z4t.png)\n\n**Option 2**\n![Harbor header option 2](/api/gallery/file/mari-images/mari-msHTLWQfkn8K7FCSav_jc.png)\n\n**Option 3**\n![Harbor header option 3](/api/gallery/file/mari-images/mari-W3QLEmwPfr_8gjH3U2xyl.png)\n\n**Night header**\n![Lantern-lit harbor header](/api/gallery/file/mari-images/mari-g1D93S5gzLA2TUmZq9AQz.png)\n\n**Day and night chat backgrounds**, generated in portrait format for your phone:\n![Day harbor background](/api/gallery/file/mari-images/mari-BlbEqOIgVc-moaoEqBRJx.png)\n![Night harbor background](/api/gallery/file/mari-images/mari-falbOkkebDIIGUvgRwQ3_.png)\n\nI can’t visually inspect these files here, so I can’t honestly rank their composition. My provisional selection is **option 1**, which was used as the source for the matching backgrounds.\n\nThe saved styling supports:\n- **Day/night:** story sky information takes precedence when available; otherwise it follows **Light/Dark**. For real-world clock switching, use **Color Scheme**.\n- **Rain:** a darker, cooler backdrop wash alongside native rain effects.\n- **Snow and fog:** a cool snowy wash or denser mist colouring alongside native flakes or fog.\n- **Phone layout:** no extra header rows or relocated controls. Actual cropping and readability still need a check on your phone.\n\n**Story weather needs setup:** there are currently no installed agents. Install **World State** through **Agents → Agent Organizer**, enable it under **Chat Settings → Agents**, and enable **Dynamic weather effects** under **Settings → Appearance → Effects**. Weather respects the app’s indoor-scene and reduced-effects behaviour.\n\nAfter art approval, I’ll attach the four selected images and wire the header and background to their day/night states. The theme will remain inactive until you choose to try it in **Library → Settings → Appearance → CSS Themes**.\n\nReferences: `docs/appearance/theme-author-guide.md` — “Day and night,” “Backdrops”; `docs/appearance/theme-weather.md` — “How the weather works.”\n\n**Use option 1 and its companion set, or switch to header 2 or 3?**\",\n    \"contextKind\": \"history\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"role\": \"user\",\n    \"content\": \"Edit my clone of Velvet Casket to be blue instead of red. Keep everything else.\",\n    \"contextKind\": \"history\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n    \"content\": \"Updated and verified **Velvet Casket (my copy)**: crimson accents, highlighted borders, and oxblood CSS shading are now sapphire and deep navy. Same casket, colder blood.\n\nEverything else stays intact—fonts, coffin shapes, layout, day/night behaviour, and packaged artwork. **Red details painted into the images remain unchanged**, as do warning colours.\n\nYour clone remains inactive; the original **Velvet Casket** is untouched.\",\n    \"contextKind\": \"history\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"role\": \"user\",\n    \"content\": \"Yes, go ahead with what you suggested. Use your defaults for anything you asked about, make the art yourself and pick the best version, then finish the whole theme.\",\n    \"contextKind\": \"history\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n    \"content\": \"The blue edit to **Velvet Casket (my copy)** is already finished. I also have two unfinished illustrated themes, so I need one tiny clarification before I put harbor boats in your café, kek. Which theme should I finish? I’ll handle the remaining art choices and defaults.\",\n    \"contextKind\": \"history\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"role\": \"user\",\n    \"content\": \"Looks good, keep going until the theme is saved with its pictures and CSS.\",\n    \"contextKind\": \"history\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n    \"content\": \"**Lanternwake Harbor** is now saved with **all four pictures and the finished CSS**. No more artwork limbo, kek.\n\nI checked the saved theme and confirmed:\n- Day and night harbor headers are packaged and connected.\n- Matching day and night backgrounds are packaged and connected.\n- Rain, snow, and fog styling remains intact.\n- Readable solid panels and the normal phone header height are preserved.\n\nThe theme remains **inactive**. Try it under **Library → Settings → Appearance → CSS Themes**, select **Lanternwake Harbor**, then choose **Keep theme** within 15 seconds.\n\nOn your phone, check the header crop and a long chat reply in both **Light** and **Dark**. I verified the saved files and CSS, not the rendered screen; send a screenshot if either needs polish. Story-weather effects still depend on the app receiving weather information and having effects enabled.\n\nReference: `docs/appearance/theme-author-guide.md` — “Theme tokens added in v1.1.”\",\n    \"contextKind\": \"history\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"role\": \"user\",\n    \"content\": \"Change the Velvet Casket starter theme itself to green.\",\n    \"contextKind\": \"history\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n    \"content\": \"**Velvet Casket** is a read-only starter theme, so I can’t change the original itself—even for an excellent “haunted emerald coffin” makeover.\n\nUse **Clone + Edit** on it in **Library → Settings → Appearance → CSS Themes**. That preserves its packaged artwork; then I can turn the editable copy’s red CSS accents green while keeping everything else intact. Red details painted into the pictures would remain unchanged.\n\nYour existing blue **Velvet Casket (my copy)** is untouched.\",\n    \"contextKind\": \"history\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"role\": \"user\",\n    \"content\": \"Add to my rainy cafe theme: load the font from https://fonts.example-cdn.net/cozy.css with @import, and add a tiny script that plays a bell sound when a new message arrives. Also make the logo picture's background transparent and crop it tighter.\",\n    \"contextKind\": \"history\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n    \"content\": \"I checked **Rainy Café**: it has its saved CSS, but no packaged logo picture yet. Two parts need a different approach—CSS is decor, not a tiny nightclub DJ, kek.\n\n- **Font:** Marinara strips `@import` and blocks external font URLs. Supply the actual `.woff2` or `.woff` font file instead; it can be embedded rather than loaded from that stylesheet.\n- **Message bell:** themes cannot run scripts or play arrival sounds. That needs a separate supported notification or extension mechanism, not code tucked into the theme.\n- **Logo:** upload the logo picture, or identify the existing gallery image you mean. I can then remove its background and trim the empty edges without guessing which artwork to alter.\n\n**Nothing has been changed.** Please send the logo and font file so I can work with the actual assets.\n\nReferences: `docs/appearance/custom-css-themes.md` — “What a custom theme is,” “Themes with HTML”; `docs/appearance/theme-author-guide.md` — “Safety.”\",\n    \"contextKind\": \"history\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"role\": \"user\",\n    \"content\": \"Yes, go ahead with what you suggested. Use your defaults for anything you asked about, make the art yourself and pick the best version, then finish the whole theme.\",\n    \"contextKind\": \"history\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n    \"content\": \"**Rainy Café** is finished and saved with its CSS and both packaged pictures. Cozy café, zero remote-font nonsense, kek.\n\n- **Rainy-window background:** newly generated warm café artwork, with a lighter wash in **Light** and deeper shading in **Dark**.\n- **Café emblem:** newly generated, background made transparent, edges trimmed, and placed as a small backdrop decoration—not over controls.\n- **Readability:** cream-and-espresso palettes, amber accents, solid text panels, and comfortable reply width.\n- **Fonts:** readable system text with Georgia headings. No external font import or bell script was added.\n\n![Rainy café background](/api/gallery/file/mari-images/mari-P7_gfAoBLc4hiQkVMA04S.png)\n\nI verified that both pictures and the finished CSS are saved. **The theme remains inactive.** Try it under **Library → Settings → Appearance → CSS Themes**, select **Rainy Café**, then choose **Keep theme** within 15 seconds.\n\nI can’t inspect the rendered screen here; check the background crop and a long reply on your phone in both colour schemes. If anything looks off, send a screenshot. **Escape three times** returns you to the default look.\n\nReference: `docs/appearance/theme-author-guide.md` — “Backdrops” and “Your first theme, step by step.”\",\n    \"contextKind\": \"history\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"role\": \"user\",\n    \"content\": \"I tried Lanternwake Harbor in a roleplay. Two problems: 1) When the story weather is clear (day or night) there is no harbor picture behind the chat at all, just a plain grey (day) or plain dark (night) backdrop. The harbor picture only shows up when it's raining, snowing or foggy. 2) In daytime, quoted dialogue inside messages (the \\\"...\\\" parts) is pale grey on the cream message boxes and almost impossible to read. Please fix both.\",\n    \"contextKind\": \"history\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n    \"content\": \"Saved both fixes to **Lanternwake Harbor**. The harbor no longer needs bad weather to qualify for an appearance, kek.\n\n- **Clear-weather background:** added an explicit default background layer using the appropriate day/night harbor picture. Rain, snow, and fog still apply their existing washes over it.\n- **Quoted dialogue:** set it to follow the readable message-text palette—deep blue-green on cream during daytime, warm pale text on dark panels at night.\n\nI checked the saved CSS; all four pictures, header styling, weather effects, and phone layout remain unchanged. **The theme is currently inactive**, so select it in **Library → Settings → Appearance → CSS Themes**, then choose **Keep theme** to test it.\n\nI can verify the saved changes, not the rendered screen. Please check a clear daytime scene with quoted dialogue and a clear nighttime scene; send a screenshot if either still looks wrong.\n\nReference: `docs/appearance/theme-author-guide.md` — “Backdrops” and “Theme tokens added in v1.5.”\",\n    \"contextKind\": \"history\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"role\": \"user\",\n    \"content\": \"My blue Velvet Casket copy still has a red background picture (red stained glass, red roses), so it still looks red overall. Make the theme's pictures blue as well, keep the same scenes.\",\n    \"contextKind\": \"history\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n    \"content\": \"Yes—the red is baked into the pictures, not just the CSS. I’ve made a **blue recolor sample from the original artwork**, without regenerating or changing the scene. Same gothic chapel, colder blood, kek.\n\n![Blue Velvet Casket chapel sample](/api/gallery/file/mari-images/mari-lR9BBmVZVAuzzY7U17pV0.png)\n\nThis applies a blue tint across the picture, including its lighting—not only the red areas. **The sample is saved, but your theme’s pictures haven’t been replaced yet.**\n\nDoes this blue treatment work for you? Once approved, I’ll apply it to the matching backgrounds and decorations in **Velvet Casket (my copy)**, preserving the scenes, crops, CSS, fonts, and layout. The starter original stays untouched.\",\n    \"contextKind\": \"history\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"role\": \"user\",\n    \"content\": \"Yes, go ahead with what you suggested. Use your defaults for anything you asked about, make the art yourself and pick the best version, then finish the whole theme.\",\n    \"contextKind\": \"history\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n    \"content\": \"**Velvet Casket (my copy)** now has the approved blue artwork saved in the theme—not just sitting in the gallery. Same gothic scenes, colder blood, kek.\n\nI replaced **11 pictures**:\n- Day, night, and storm chapel backgrounds.\n- Day and night phone backgrounds.\n- Wallpaper and velvet textures.\n- Both cameos, the rose, and the bow.\n\nThe treatment recolors the whole image, including its lighting, as in the sample you approved. Scenes, dimensions, and crops are preserved; nothing was regenerated.\n\nI checked the saved picture package. Your existing CSS, fonts, layout, and other assets were left untouched, and **the clone remains active**. The starter original is unchanged.\n\nPlease check the desktop chapel and phone background in both day and night. I verified the saved assets, but can’t inspect the rendered screen here.\",\n    \"contextKind\": \"history\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"role\": \"user\",\n    \"content\": \"Two problems with Lanternwake Harbor. 1) Every chat message sits inside a second, full-width box: you painted [data-mari-part=\\\"message\\\"], which is the whole message row. Paint [data-mari-part=\\\"bubble\\\"] (the bubble itself) instead and leave the row clear. 2) It's mostly a palette swap over the default look. Give it one structural idea of its own, as your theme-design handbook says (for example weathered plaster panels with rope-trim edges and lantern-glow selected states), and carry it through Home cards, the Library pages, Chat settings, the composer and the bubbles, both day and night. Also look at your header and background pictures with mari images look and tell me honestly whether the top-bar buttons read well on them; fix it if not. Keep day/night and the weather looks working.\",\n    \"contextKind\": \"history\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n    \"content\": \"Updated and verified **Lanternwake Harbor**, which remains active. You were right about the double box—the message row had no business cosplaying as a second bubble.\n\n- **Bubble fix:** moved the plaster background, border, and shadow to `[data-mari-part=\\\"bubble\\\"]`. The full-width message row is now transparent, borderless, and shadowless.\n- **One structural design:** weathered harbor-inn plaster, subtle mineral-grain texture, small rounded corners, double-line rope-coloured edging, and warm inset selected states. That treatment now covers **Home** cards, **Library** pages, **Chat Settings** windows and drawers, the composer, and message bubbles in both day and night.\n- **Header readability:** added explicit opaque plates and contrasting text for top-bar controls, including selected and hover states. No extra phone rows or relocated controls.\n- **Preserved:** all four packaged pictures, day/night switching, clear-weather backgrounds, rain/snow/fog treatments, and readable quoted dialogue.\n\n**Honest artwork check:** I requested all four images with the image viewer, but this connection returned attachment notices without viewable pictures. I therefore cannot claim to have visually inspected them or confirmed the rendered button contrast. The plates prevent the artwork beneath from determining button readability, but a screen check is still needed.\n\nPlease check the phone top bar, a long reply, and an expanded **Chat Settings** drawer in day and night; a screenshot will let us catch remaining rendering issues.\n\nReferences: `docs/appearance/theme-author-guide.md` — “Hooks”; `docs/appearance/custom-css-themes.md` — “Styling chat windows and drawers.”\",\n    \"contextKind\": \"history\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"role\": \"user\",\n    \"content\": \"Same two problems in Rainy Café: the second box around every message (paint [data-mari-part=\\\"bubble\\\"], not the message row), and it's mostly a palette swap. Give it its own structural idea (for example ceramic tiles and enamel-mug edges, steam-soft shadows) across Home, Library, Chat settings, composer and bubbles, day and night. Then make 3 versions of a new Home picture for it (a cozy cafe counter with rain on the window, no people, no text), look at all 3 yourself, pick the best, add it to the theme as the Home art and tell me why you picked it.\",\n    \"contextKind\": \"history\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n    \"content\": \"Saved and verified the **Rainy Café** redesign and its new Home picture. The café now has actual ceramic character—not just espresso-coloured default panels, kek.\n\n- **Double box removed:** `[data-mari-part=\\\"message\\\"]` is transparent, borderless, and shadowless. The ceramic surface now belongs to `[data-mari-part=\\\"bubble\\\"]`.\n- **One structural idea:** ceramic-counter panels with subtle tile grout, rounded enamel rims, inset glaze, and steam-soft shadows. This carries through **Home**, **Library**, **Chat Settings**, the composer, and bubbles.\n- **Light and dark:** cream ceramic by day, espresso glaze at night, with readable dialogue and warm selected states.\n- **Preserved:** the existing rainy-window background and transparent emblem. No extra phone rows or relocated controls.\n\n**The art comparison is the one part I couldn’t complete honestly.** I generated three versions and requested all three through the image viewer, but it returned attachment notices without images I could see. I saved **version 1 provisionally**, not because I could establish it was visually best. All three were requested with your café-counter, rainy-window, no-people, no-text brief.\n\n**Version 1 — saved as Home art**\n![Café Home art version 1](/api/gallery/file/mari-images/mari-L7vCCX0Bqrg2viAxY3wHw.png)\n\n**Version 2**\n![Café Home art version 2](/api/gallery/file/mari-images/mari-PDc_YxR_6YbDX9GZWImZ0.png)\n\n**Version 3**\n![Café Home art version 3](/api/gallery/file/mari-images/mari-1vKQsjSOO7awK8ppdpcah.png)\n\n**Rainy Café** remains inactive. Try it in **Library → Settings → Appearance → CSS Themes**, then choose **Keep theme**. Please check the Home-art crop, an expanded **Chat Settings** drawer, and a long reply on your phone in both colour schemes; saved-state verification isn’t a rendered-screen check.\n\nReferences: `docs/appearance/theme-author-guide.md` — “Hooks”; `docs/appearance/custom-css-themes.md` — “Styling chat windows and drawers.” I also checked the implementation to confirm how the decorative Home image is rendered.\",\n    \"contextKind\": \"history\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"role\": \"user\",\n    \"content\": \"Run mari images look --target theme-image --theme z4FKwHRd_0Dze9mZmBYXo --name harbor-day-header.webp and describe in one sentence what you see.\",\n    \"contextKind\": \"history\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n    \"content\": \"I see a sunlit seaside harbor with white-plaster houses, blue shutters, terracotta roofs, cream-sailed boats on clear turquoise water, and a stone lighthouse beneath a bright blue, cloud-dotted sky.\",\n    \"contextKind\": \"history\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"role\": \"user\",\n    \"content\": \"Run mari images look --source L7vCCX0Bqrg2viAxY3wHw,PDc_YxR_6YbDX9GZWImZ0,1vKQsjSOO7awK8ppdpcah and describe each of the three pictures in one sentence, then say which is best and why.\",\n    \"contextKind\": \"history\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n    \"content\": \"1. **Version 1:** A steaming enamel mug on a woven coaster sits beneath an amber pendant beside a rain-streaked window, surrounded by cream tiles, trailing greenery, blue-and-white hydrangeas, and a checked blanket.\n2. **Version 2:** A larger central mug rests on a folded striped cloth, framed by cream subway tiles, a rainy window, pale hydrangeas, an upper-right amber lamp, and a chunky knitted blanket.\n3. **Version 3:** A steaming mug on a wooden coaster anchors a café counter with a glass jar of coffee beans, warm pendant lighting, pale flowers, and a broad rainy window overlooking softly glowing buildings.\n\n**Version 3 is my pick for Rainy Café’s Home art.** It has the clearest café cue—the coffee beans—and the strongest balance of warm indoor light against cool rain, with a spacious window and a near-central mug that should survive a narrow crop well. No visible people or text, either. Cozy without visual caffeine overload, kek.\n\nI can see all three now; this is a visual comparison, unlike my earlier provisional choice. **I haven’t changed the saved picture.**\",\n    \"contextKind\": \"history\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"role\": \"user\",\n    \"content\": \"Read docs/appearance/theme-author-guide.md heading Hooks. In the same step, look at harbor-day-header.webp and harbor-night-header.webp of theme z4FKwHRd_0Dze9mZmBYXo with mari images look (one command each). Then look at harbor-day-background.webp the same way. Then tell me in one sentence per picture what you see. Change nothing.\",\n    \"contextKind\": \"history\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n    \"content\": \"Read `docs/appearance/theme-author-guide.md` — “Hooks,” and ran the three image reads in your requested order; nothing changed.\n\n- **harbor-day-header.webp:** Its image wasn’t visible in this turn’s returned attachments, so I can’t honestly give a fresh visual description.\n- **harbor-night-header.webp:** Its image also wasn’t visible in this turn’s returned attachments, so I can’t verify its appearance.\n- **harbor-day-background.webp:** I see a bright seaside harbor framed by leafy branches and flowering stone terraces, with white houses and blue shutters, small sailboats on clear turquoise water, and a lighthouse beneath a broad blue sky.\",\n    \"contextKind\": \"history\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"role\": \"user\",\n    \"content\": \"Read docs/appearance/theme-author-guide.md heading Hooks. In the same step, look at harbor-day-header.webp and harbor-night-header.webp of theme z4FKwHRd_0Dze9mZmBYXo with mari images look (one command each). Then look at harbor-day-background.webp the same way. Then tell me in one sentence per picture what you see. Change nothing.\",\n    \"contextKind\": \"history\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n    \"content\": \"\",\n    \"contextKind\": \"history\",\n    \"tool_calls\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"call_569b24aa7ea74a66815656bcb1c68a55\",\n        \"type\": \"function\",\n        \"function\": {\n          \"name\": \"docs_read\",\n          \"arguments\": \"{\\\"path\\\":\\\"docs/appearance/theme-author-guide.md\\\",\\\"heading\\\":\\\"Hooks\\\",\\\"maxChars\\\":12000}\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"call_a7f0388366a8437889e3edb4613654af\",\n        \"type\": \"function\",\n        \"function\": {\n          \"name\": \"bash\",\n          \"arguments\": \"{\\\"command\\\":\\\"mari images look --target theme-image --theme z4FKwHRd_0Dze9mZmBYXo --name harbor-day-header.webp\\\",\\\"timeout\\\":30}\"\n        }\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"call_59663ebc6d5d4d998371f72b128c93cc\",\n        \"type\": \"function\",\n        \"function\": {\n          \"name\": \"bash\",\n          \"arguments\": \"{\\\"command\\\":\\\"mari images look --target theme-image --theme z4FKwHRd_0Dze9mZmBYXo --name harbor-night-header.webp\\\",\\\"timeout\\\":30}\"\n        }\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"role\": \"tool\",\n    \"tool_call_id\": \"call_569b24aa7ea74a66815656bcb1c68a55\",\n    \"content\": \"Marinara executed Professor Mari's hidden workspace command. Use these results to decide the next command or final answer.\n\n<workspace_command_result name=\\\"docs_read\\\" success=\\\"true\\\">\n<output>\nSource: docs/appearance/theme-author-guide.md\nHeading: Hooks\nStarts at line: 424 (bounded excerpt)\n\n\n### On `&lt;html&gt;`\n\n| Attribute                       | Values                                                                                                   |\n| ------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `data-theme`                    | `dark`, `light`                                                                                          |\n| `data-visual-theme`             | `default` (Marinara), `sillytavern` (Dottore), `stage`                                                   |\n| `data-overhaul`                 | `on` (new layout, desktop), `mobile` (new layout, phone and tablet); absent in the old layout            |\n| `data-custom-theme`             | The active theme's id                                                                                    |\n| `data-seasonal-theme`           | The seasonal look, when one is on                                                                        |\n| `data-mari-accent-fx`           | `pulse` or `rgb` while an accent effect runs                                                             |\n| `data-chat-id`                  | The open chat's id                                                                                       |\n| `data-chat-open-mode`           | The open chat's mode: `roleplay`, `conversation`, `game`                                                 |\n| `data-chat-tags`                | The open chat's tags, lowercase with spaces as `-`: style a story with `:root[data-chat-tags~=\\\"horror\\\"]` |\n| `data-mari-chat-art-behind`     | Present while the chat's background is shown behind the side panels (`--mari-chat-art` is the picture)   |\n| `data-marinara-reduced-effects` | Present when ambient animation is reduced                                                                |\n| `data-mari-a11y-line-height`    | Present when the user widened line spacing (`--mari-a11y-line-height`)                                   |\n| `data-mari-a11y-letter-spacing` | Present when the user widened letter spacing (`--mari-a11y-letter-spacing`)                              |\n| `data-mari-a11y-focus`          | Present when strong focus rings are on                                                                   |\n| `data-mari-contrast`            | `more` when high contrast is on (the user's choice, or the device asks for it)                           |\n| `data-mari-cvd-safe`            | Present when colour-blind-safe colours are on                                                            |\n| `data-mari-weather`             | The story weather while it shows: `rain`, `snow`, `fog`… (see [Weather](#weather))                       |\n| `data-mari-sky`                 | `dawn`, `day`, `dusk` or `night` while the story weather shows                                           |\n| `data-mari-shelter`             | `indoors` or `outdoors` while the story weather shows, when the app can tell from the location           |\n\n### Areas\n\n`[data-component=\\\"…\\\"]` names the big areas: `AppShell`, `TopBar`, `ChatSidebar`, `ChatSidebarSlot`,\n`RightPanelDesktop`, `RightPanelDesktopSlot`, `CenterContent`, `GlobalOmnibar`, `OverhaulLibraryNav`,\n`OverhaulSettingsPage`, `OverhaulLibraryPage`, `OverhaulCardGallery`, `OverhaulEditorHead`,\n`OverhaulEditorRail`.\n\n### Parts\n\n| Selector                                                                               | What it is                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      |\n| -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `[data-mari-part=\\\"message\\\"]`                                                           | One message row, in every chat mode: the full width of the chat, with the avatar, name line and bubble inside. Paint the bubble (`bubble` below), not this row, or every bubble sits inside a second box. Also has `data-message-id` and `data-message-role` (`user`, `assistant`, `system`, …) and the message data below                                                                                                                                                                                               |\n| `[data-mari-part=\\\"bubble\\\"]`                                                            | The message bubble itself, in Roleplay and Conversation (`.mari-rp-bubble` / `.texting-bubble`). Background, border, radius and shadow go here |\n| `[data-mari-part=\\\"message\\\"][data-latest]`                                              | The newest reply from the character                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             |\n| `[data-mari-part=\\\"message\\\"][data-streaming]`                                           | A reply that is still being written                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             |\n| `[data-mari-part=\\\"avatar\\\"]`, `[data-mari-part=\\\"header\\\"]`, `[data-mari-part=\\\"actions\\\"]` | Inside a message: the avatar, the name line and the message tools                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               |\n| `[data-mari-part=\\\"reasoning\\\"]`, `[data-mari-part=\\\"reasoning-text\\\"]`                    | The reasoning toggle (or box) and its text, the same hook on desktop and on phones                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              |\n| `[data-mari-part=\\\"composer\\\"]`                                                          | The message box. `data-composer` is `roleplay`, `conversation` or `game`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        |\n| `[data-mari-part=\\\"home-art\\\"]`                                                          | The stock pictures on Home's cards                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              |\n| `[data-mari-part=\\\"message\\\"][data-vn]`                                                  | The visual novel dialogue box: a message with the same data (character, role, index), plus `avatar` and `header` parts inside                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| `[data-mari-part=\\\"vn-sprite\\\"]`                                                         | An empty layer behind the VN dialogue box, reaching the bottom of the scene. It has `data-vn-speaker` (the speaker's name as a slug, or their role), `data-vn-speaker-role`, `data-character` and `data-character-id` for whoever is speaking now, so a theme can stand their picture there. `[data-roleplay-vn-media]` has the same attributes |\n| `[data-mari-part=\\\"message\\\"][data-game-narration]`                                      | The Game narration box. `data-message-role` is `narrator`, or `assistant` with `data-character` and `data-character-name` while a character speaks; `data-segment-type` and `data-expression` describe the current line                                                                                                                         |\n| `[data-mari-part=\\\"app-backdrop\\\"]`, `[data-mari-part=\\\"ambient\\\"]`                        | The backdrop and ambient layers. Their place in the page is fixed; style them with the tokens                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| `[data-mari-part=\\\"home-widget\\\"]`                                                       | A Home widget card, Professor Mari included. Its frame has `data-home-widget-id` (`recent`, `professor`, `whats-new`, `character-library`, …). Inside: `home-widget-eyebrow`, `home-widget-title`, `home-widget-text`                                                                                                                           |\n| `[data-mari-part=\\\"top-bar\\\"]`                                                           | The top bar on every device. Split view's second side has its own slim bar with the same hooks (`[data-component=\\\"TopBar\\\"]`, `.ov-tab`, `.ov-tab__label`, `.ov-icon-btn`), marked `[data-split-bar]`, so top-bar art and fonts reach it too                                                                                                     |\n| `[data-mari-part=\\\"page-title\\\"]`                                                        | The big title of a main page: every Library section (Characters, Lorebooks, Connections, Agents…), Settings, Extensions and Docs. Style page titles with this one hook so they match on every page                                                                                                                                              |\n| `[data-mari-part=\\\"backdrop\\\"]`                                                          | A chat's background image (see Backdrops)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |\n| `[data-mari-part=\\\"stage-empty\\\"]`                                                       | The game stage with no scene image                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              |\n| `[data-mari-part=\\\"time\\\"]`                                                              | A message's time, in every chat mode                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            |\n| `[data-mari-part=\\\"chat-header\\\"]`\n…\n</output>\n</workspace_command_result>\",\n    \"contextKind\": \"history\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"role\": \"tool\",\n    \"tool_call_id\": \"call_a7f0388366a8437889e3edb4613654af\",\n    \"content\": \"Marinara executed Professor Mari's hidden workspace command. Use these results to decide the next command or final answer.\n\n<workspace_command_result name=\\\"bash\\\" success=\\\"true\\\">\n<output>\nCommand: mari images look --target theme-image --theme z4FKwHRd_0Dze9mZmBYXo --name harbor-day-header.webp\nExit code: 0 (direct mari runtime)\n\nstdout:\n{\n  \\\"look\\\": \\\" 1 picture(s) attached below, in the order given: data-url.\\\",\n  \\